  {"id": "d6", "q": "In one sentence each: what do L2, L1, and dropout do differently?",
   "model": "L2 shrinks weights smoothly (Gaussian prior / weight decay). L1 drives many weights to exact zero via diamond corners (Laplace / sparse). Dropout randomly zeros units in training to force redundancy."},
